# Repository-root .dockerignore — used when a service is built with the
# repo root as its context (marketing-ui: the build needs CHANGELOG.md +
# .git to bake status.json; api: the build bakes the changelog's top line
# into /web10/VERSION for the node's update check). Tuned to send only what
# those builds touch while keeping the door open for other services (ui,
# social) that may later move to a repo-root context too.

# Universal dev/build crud — never needed in any image build.
**/node_modules
**/dist
!sdk/dist
**/build
**/.cache
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/*.log
**/*.pid

# Editor + OS noise.
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
**/.vscode
*.swp
*.swo

# Secrets + local state never belong in an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.local
.gitlab
.github
.dockerignore

# Conductor / agent scratch — never in the image.
.conductor
.context

# Heavy marketing subprojects that ship their own Dockerfile / context
# and never bake the marketing-ui bundle. Excluded here only to keep the
# marketing-ui context small; their own `context:` is unaffected.
marketing/web10-social/node_modules
marketing/web10-cli/node_modules
mobile/node_modules

# Editor docs + research dumps the build never reads. EXCEPT the changelog:
# the api image bakes its top line into /web10/VERSION at build time
# (api/Dockerfile — the node's update check, KB setup/update-check.md).
knowledge-base/**/*.md
!knowledge-base/changelogs/CHANGELOG.md
ai-pack/**/*.md
e2e/screenshots
e2e/.playwright

# .git: kept intact in full so `git rev-parse`/`git log` work at build
# time (build-status.sh needs the live commit SHA + date). A normal
# /opt/web10 clone is shallow on the box's Portainer GitOps pull and tiny
# in practice; do NOT exclude .git/objects/pack or rev-parse will FAIL.
